No increase in monster difficulty. What it did (in 3.0.10; haven't
checked earlier versions) was:

* increase monster creation when deep or after killing Rodney
* cause you to rub out engravings just by standing there
* cause Rodney to resurrect or other nasty things to happen occasionally
  after killing him
* cause a mysterious force to sometimes hinder the ascent out of
  Gehennom
* cause cursed weapons and rings not to slip from your hands
* reduce the chance of surviving choking from 95% to 5%
* reduce the effect of exceptional strength on carrying capacity
* add the 'summon nasty' monster spell
* create wands of wishing with 1-3 charges rather than a fixed 3
* allow unhidden hiders out of sight to rehide.
* increase prayer timeout after crowning and after killing the Wizard
* remove the one-warning before angering gods
* have a chance of angering shopkeepers who thought you owed them money
* give spellbooks limited uses
* give spells a chance of failure based on Luck, INT, and spell level.
* not put an amulet of life saving in your initial inventory.

In short, almost everything from HARD is what's now considered to be
the basic game.

